 "about_text": "ROSEGALLERY is a Los Angeles-area gallery founded in 1991 by Rose Shoshana at the Bergamot Station Arts Center in Santa Monica. The program centers on modern and contemporary photography, spanning works that draw on the medium's history as well as contemporary photo-based art. Shoshana, who trained at Art Center College of Design and worked in editorial photography before opening the gallery, has built relationships with artists such as William Eggleston, Bruce Davidson, and Graciela Iturbide, and has collaborated with institutions including the Getty Museum and Tate Modern. The gallery represents a roster of established and emerging photographers and lens-based artists, and regularly presents work at international art fairs including Paris Photo and Photo London.",
